-- M3 fixes, B1 (C19): a genuinely malformed pattern (`a\(` opens a
-- group and never closes it, so Str.regexp itself raises Failure) is
-- a DISTINCT runtime error (Regex_bad_pattern), never the same
-- silent no-match a benign miss produces.  Pre-fix this printed
-- `false` and exited 0 (the classic fail-open shape for a guard with
-- a typo'd pattern), recorded in dev/M3-FIXES-LOG.md.
eval regexTest "a\\(" "aaa"
